  "flag": "(e)+(d) The fire-severity figure has a SEVERITY vs INTENSITY definition box that states the answer outright, so the item only tests reading the figure. The figure also says high severity = 'Most trees killed' while reporting Big Basin as ~77% high severity, which clashes with T5-11/M-14 ('many old-growth redwoods survived'). The 77% mapping measured canopy loss, not tree death. Fix: drop the definition box for this item (or ask an application question), and change 'Most trees killed' to 'Most canopy burned' plus a footnote that many redwoods resprouted."
